<title>USA: Rite Aid files shelf of $600 mln debt/stock.</title>
<headline>Rite Aid files shelf of $600 mln debt/stock.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rite Aid Corp said Wednesday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $600 million debt securities, preferred and common stock and warrants.</p>
<p>The Camp Hill, Pa., based company said net proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>When combined with previous registrations, Rite Aid will have a total offering of $1 billion, the filing said.</p>
<p>Rite Aid is a retail drug store chain in the United States.</p>
</text>
